course: dictionary
lesson: 563
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. August with a capital A is the eighth month of the year. Written with a small a, august means grand, important and respected. The context tells you which one you are reading.
explain: «Swifts come to Britain in May and leave in August» is about the month, because it names a time of the year. Read the words around the word: they are the clues.
explain: Now try a sentence with the small a: «The august judge walked into the hall, and everyone stood up.» Swap in your meaning: «The grand judge walked into the hall» still makes sense, so august means grand here.
fact: August is the eighth month of the year, with 31 days.
fact: August comes after July and before September.
fact: Small a august means grand, important and respected, as in «an august group of scientists».
fact: August is summer in the USA, UK, Canada and Ireland, but winter in Australia and New Zealand.
fact: To count the months on your knuckles, July and August sit on two knuckles side by side.
exercise: Which month comes straight after July? | June | September | *August | October
exercise: In «The august judge walked into the hall», what does august mean? | The eighth month of the year | *Grand and respected | Tiny and quiet | Cold and wet
exercise: In «Swifts leave Britain in August», what kind of word is August? | A type of bird | A word meaning grand | *The name of a month | A kind of weather
test: In Australia and New Zealand, August is which season? | Autumn | *Winter | Summer | Spring
test: What does august mean in «an august group of scientists met in the hall»? | Very hot | The eighth month of the year | *Grand and important | Very small
exam: How can you tell whether «August» is the month or «august» means grand? | Both mean the same, so it does not matter | You count the letters | Capital A means grand, small a means the month | *Capital A means the month, small a means grand
